   139	- The entry domain is exactly modeled string values `str(CS)`; non-string
   140	  arguments are outside the HumanEval signature contract.  There is no hidden
   141	  restriction on length, number of words, leading/trailing spaces, or repeated
   142	  spaces.
   143	- The reference model represents characters by integer codes and the delimiter
   144	  by ASCII code `32`, matching the prompt's ASCII-order wording.  The symbolic
   145	  theorem accepts arbitrary code sequences; concrete string literals in this
   146	  semantics are ASCII-only.
